{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"New Jersey Security Deposit Law deposit cap and return","requirement":"A landlord may not demand a security deposit above one and one-half times one month's rent, may raise an existing deposit by no more than 10% in any year, and must return the deposit plus interest within 30 days after the tenancy ends.","key_value":"1.5 months' rent; 10% annual increase cap","coverage_conditions":"Residential rentals in New Jersey; seasonal use or rental of not more than 125 consecutive days is exempt.","applicability":{"conditions":[],"per_tenancy":"Applies to residential tenancies; seasonal use or rental of 125 consecutive days or fewer is exempt from the account and deposit rules.","coverage_quotes":[]},"exemptions":"Seasonal use or rental for a term of not more than 125 consecutive days; a landlord is not required to collect any security deposit.","penalty":"If the deposit is not returned within 30 days, the tenant may sue for double the amount wrongly withheld, plus court costs and reasonable attorney's fees.","effective_date":null,"valid_through":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.2","quoted_span":"The maximum-security deposit to be collected by the landlord cannot be more than one and one-half times one month’s rent ( N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.2 ). It can be less. Any additional yearly security deposit increase may not exceed 10% of the current security deposit.","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.75,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Safe Housing Act security deposit return after domestic violence termination","requirement":"When a tenant ends a lease under the Safe Housing Act because of domestic violence, the landlord must make the security deposit plus interest available within 15 business days and notify the tenant in writing within three business days where to collect it.","key_value":"15 business days","coverage_conditions":"Tenants who terminate a residential lease under the New Jersey Safe Housing Act after documenting domestic violence; not transient or seasonal rentals.","applicability":{"conditions":[],"per_tenancy":"Applies where a tenant terminates the lease under the Safe Housing Act after documenting domestic violence; does not apply to transient or seasonal rentals.","coverage_quotes":[]},"exemptions":"Transient or seasonal rentals.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"valid_through":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-9.6","quoted_span":"Within 15 business days after the lease  is terminated, the landlord shall make available the return of the tenant’s security deposit, plus any interest earned, to the tenant or the tenant’s agent.","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.7,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-01","n_rules":2,"note":null}

